# Viewing Processes in Linux

Processes are running programs in the system.  
Linux provides the `ps` command to display information about active processes.

---

## ps vs ps -e

| Command | Meaning |
|---------|----------|
| `ps` | shows processes running in the current terminal session only |
| `ps -e` | shows ALL running processes in the system |
| `ps -ef` | shows all processes in full format (detailed view) |
| `ps aux` | shows all processes in user-oriented format (common usage) |

